# Auto-detect text files and normalize line endings.
#
# `eol=lf` pins the WORKING TREE to LF as well, not just the stored blobs, which
# is what stops "LF will be replaced by CRLF the next time Git touches it": that
# warning is the conversion announcing itself, so the fix is to remove the
# conversion rather than reverse it.
#
# Not CRLF, deliberately. 364 PHP files carry heredocs, and a heredoc takes the
# file's own line endings into the string — under CRLF every one of them would
# silently emit \r\n in generated HTML, SQL and mail, and every test asserting
# "\n" would break. LF also makes a Windows checkout byte-identical to CI.
#
# This overrides core.autocrlf, so it holds for every clone without anyone
# having to configure their machine.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Ensure shell scripts use LF (required for bash/sh)
*.sh text eol=lf
scripts/* text eol=lf

# Binary files
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.eot binary
*.pdf binary
